<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Val-ès-Dunes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1047">1047</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Val-ès-Dunes was fought in 1047 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caen">Caen</a>, where the young Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> and his overlord King Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> defeated a coalition of rebel barons from western Normandy led by Guy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. It was William's first major victory and the beginning of his firm control of the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-val-es-dunes.jpg" alt="Battle of Val-ès-Dunes" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pethrus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Val_%C3%A8s_Dunes_battle-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The young William II, who succeeded his father Robert I in 1035 at the age of about seven or eight, survived a decade of baronial violence and, with the help of King Henry I of France, defeated rebel lords at the <b>Battle of Val-ès-Dunes</b> in 1047.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Duchy of Normandy · Military</a></li></ul></section>
